Claim 1 (Original): A wearable electrocardiography device, comprising:

a flexible backing having a mid-section, a distal end, and a proximal end, wherein each of the distal end and the proximal end taper inward to the mid-section, wherein the mid-section includes a first edge parallel to a second edge, and wherein the mid-section is narrower than the distal end and the proximal end;

an SpO2 sensor provided on the flexible backing;

a discontinuous adhesive layer disposed on a contact surface of the flexible backing to adhere the flexible backing to skin of a patient's chest, wherein the discontinuous adhesive layer includes a first portion disposed on the distal end and a second portion disposed on the proximal end;

a monitor recorder having a rigid housing with rounded edges on a top surface, wherein the monitor recorder is configured to    draw  power from    a battery, and wherein electrocardiographic signals are stored in the monitor recorder, the monitor recorder comprising:a flash memory;

a temperature sensor;

a wireless transceiver;

a microcontroller; and

an electrocardiographic front end circuit;

a non-conductive receptacle disposed between the skin of the patient's chest and the monitor recorder, the non-conductive receptacle comprising a battery compartment for the battery;

a circular feedback button disposed on the top surface of the housing, wherein the circular feedback button is configured to output feedback to the patient;

a flexible circuit disposed on a top surface of the flexible backing, wherein the flexible circuit comprises:an inline resistor;

a proximal circuit trace, wherein the proximal circuit trace is electrically coupled to  a   proximal  electrocardiography  electrode,  and  wherein  the  proximal electrocardiography electrode is disposed on the proximal end; and





a distal circuit trace electrically coupled to a distal electrocardiography electrode,

wherein the distal electrocardiography electrode is disposed on the distal end, and wherein the electrocardiographic front end circuit senses the electrocardiographic signals via the distal electrocardiography electrode and the proximal electrocardiography electrode.



Claim 2 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the inline resistor is disposed between the housing and the skin of the patient's chest.



Claim 3 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the wearable electrocardiography device further comprises tabs for placement of the wearable electrocardiography device on the skin of the patient's chest.



Claim 4 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the non-conductive receptacle includes a concave feature.



Claim 5 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the circular feedback button is waterproof.



Claim 6 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the housing engages the non-conductive receptacle to form a moisture-resistant seal.



Claim 7 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the non-conductive receptacle comprises a seal.



Claim 8 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 7, wherein the seal is a circular shape that surrounds an electrical pad.



Claim 9 (Original):  The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim  1, further comprising an analog-to-digital converter.







Claim 10 (Original): The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the wearable electrocardiography device senses electrocardiographic signals via a single channel.



Claim 11 (Original): The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 1, wherein the distal end and the proximal end are asymmetric about the mid-section.



Claim 12 (Original): A wearable electrocardiography device, comprising:

a monitor recorder configured to record and store electrocardiographic signals, the monitor recorder comprising:a wireless transceiver, wherein the wireless transceiver communicates via Bluetooth communications;

a microcontroller;

an electrocardiographic front end circuit; and

a flash memory;

a non-conductive receptacle disposed between skin of a patient's chest and the monitor recorder, the non-conductive receptacle comprising a battery to provide power to the monitor recorder;

a flexible backing having a mid-section, a distal end, and a proximal end, wherein the mid-section includes a first edge parallel to a second edge, and wherein the mid-section is narrower than the distal end and the proximal end;

an SpO2 sensor provided on the flexible backing;

an adhesive layer, wherein the adhesive layer is disposed on at least a portion of a first surface of the flexible backing, and wherein the adhesive layer adheres the distal end and the proximal end to the skin of the patient's chest;

a button disposed on a housing, wherein the wearable electrocardiography device is configured to output feedback to the patient to confirm that the wearable electrocardiography device is recording the electrocardiographic signals;

a physiological sensor;



a flexible circuit disposed on a second surface of the flexible backing, wherein the flexible circuit comprises:

an inline resistor;

a proximal circuit trace, wherein the proximal circuit trace is electrically coupled to  a   proximal   electrocardiography  electrode,  and  wherein  the  proximal electrocardiography electrode is disposed on the proximal end; and

a distal circuit trace electrically coupled to a distal electrocardiography electrode,

wherein the distal electrocardiography electrode is disposed on the distal end, and wherein the electrocardiographic front end circuit senses the electrocardiographic signals via the distal electrocardiography electrode and the proximal electrocardiography electrode.



Claim 13 (Original): The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 12, wherein the monitor recorder comprises a physiological sensor, and wherein the physiological sensor is a temperature sensor.



Claim 14 (Original): The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 12, wherein a physiological sensor is provided on the flexible backing.



Claim 15 (Original): The wearable electrocardiography device of Claim 12, wherein a physiological sensor is provided on the flexible backing, and wherein the physiological sensor is a blood pressure sensor.



