Claim 30 (Original): A wearable electrocardiography device, comprising:

a flexible backing having a mid-section, a distal end, and a proximal end, wherein the distal end and the proximal end are rounded on respective outer edges, wherein each of the distal end and the proximal end taper inward to the mid-section, wherein the mid-section includes a first edge parallel to a second edge, and wherein the mid-section is narrower than the distal end and the proximal end;

an SpO2 sensor provided on the flexible backing, wherein the SpO2 sensor comprises a light emitting diode and a photodiode;

an adhesive layer disposed on a contact surface of the flexible backing, wherein the adhesive layer adheres the flexible backing to skin a patient's chest, and wherein the adhesive layer is disposed only on the distal end and the proximal end of the contact surface of the flexible backing;

a monitor recorder having a rigid housing with rounded edges on a top surface, wherein the monitor recorder is configured to draw power from a battery, the monitor recorder comprising:a flash memory;

a temperature sensor;

a wireless transceiver;

a microcontroller; and





an electrocardiographic front end circuit;

a non-conductive receptacle configured to engage the monitor recorder, wherein the non- conductive receptacle comprises a battery compartment for the battery, and wherein the battery is vertically aligned with the wireless transceiver;

a waterproof circular feedback button disposed on the top surface of the housing configured to output feedback to the patient;

a flexible circuit disposed on a top surface of the flexible backing, wherein the flexible circuit comprises:

an inline resistor;

a proximal circuit trace, wherein the proximal circuit trace is electrically coupled to   a  proximal   electrocardiography  electrode,  and  wherein   the   proximal electrocardiography electrode is disposed on the proximal end; and

a distal circuit trace electrically coupled to a distal electrocardiography electrode,

wherein the distal electrocardiography electrode is disposed on the distal end, and wherein the electrocardiographic front end circuit senses electrocardiographic signals via the distal electrocardiography electrode and the proximal electrocardiography electrode.
